## 9. Key Metrics & Analytics

To evaluate product success, the following telemetry and business metrics will be tracked in our Node.js reporting backend (ensuring no borrower PII is collected).

```
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                 METRIC CATEGORIES                               |
+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| 1. Technical Performance          | - SDK Initialization Success Rate (Target: >99.9%) |
|                                   | - Average Parsing Execution Time (Target: <5s)     |
|                                   | - Crash-Free Sessions Rate (Target: >99.95%)       |
+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| 2. Parsing Accuracy & Quality     | - Intent Classification F1-Score (Target: >0.95)   |
|                                   | - Discard Rate (Spam/Non-Financial)                |
+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| 3. Business & Monetization        | - Successful Profiles Generated (Target: 500k/mo)  |
|                                   | - Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR)                  |
|                                   | - Average Revenue Per Account (ARPA)               |
+-----------------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
```

### 9.1 Technical Performance Metrics
*   **SDK Initialization Success Rate:** Target is **>99.9%**. Track initialization failures caused by dynamic library loading issues (.so files) or JNI binding errors.
*   **Average Parsing Execution Time:** Track the time taken from permission verification to final JSON generation. Target is **<5 seconds** for 90 days of SMS history.
*   **Crash-Free Sessions Rate:** Target is **>99.95%**. Monitor JNI boundary crashes or memory leaks in the Rust parser.

### 9.2 Parsing Accuracy & Quality Metrics
*   **Intent Classification F1-Score:** The TFLite model's precision and recall in categorizing financial alerts must maintain an **F1-score of >0.95** in production validation.
*   **Discard Rate:** Percentage of messages processed and classified as spam/non-financial. This helps monitor whether the pre-filtering logic is functioning correctly.

### 9.3 Business & Monetization Metrics
*   **Successful Profiles Generated:** Volume of profiles billed at $0.15. Target is **500,000 successful profiles per month** within 6 months of launch.
*   **Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR):** Calculated as `Total Successful Profiles Generated x $0.15`.
*   **Average Revenue Per Account (ARPA):** Monitor the monthly spend per fintech client to identify high-volume accounts and optimize custom tier-pricing models.

