## 6. Security, Privacy & Regulatory Compliance

### 6.1 DPDP Act 2023 & RBI Compliance Checklist

| Requirement | Implementation Status | Technical Mechanism |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Consent Architecture** | Fully Compliant | Host app must present explicit, itemized consent screens before triggering `SafeParseSDK.initialize()`. |
| **Purpose Limitation** | Fully Compliant | SDK only scans for keywords mapped to transactional alerts (e.g., UPI, credit, debit, utility). Personal chat SMS patterns are immediately ignored. |
| **Data Minimization** | Fully Compliant | Raw SMS text is processed completely in-memory (Rust/JNI stack) and never saved or transmitted. Only mathematical aggregates are written to SQLCipher and uploaded. |
| **Right to Erasure** | Fully Compliant | Exposing `clearAllData()` to trigger cryptographic deletion of the local database file and wiping keys from KeyStore. |
| **No Sideloaded Execution** | Fully Compliant | TFLite model weights are packaged static inside the Android Asset bundle, verified by APK signature verification. No dynamic code loading (DCL) is used. |

### 6.2 Key Management via Android Keystore System
To prevent unauthorized access to the SQLCipher database, the encryption key is generated and stored securely within the hardware-backed Android Keystore.

