# Production-Grade Sprint Plan: On-Device Privacy-Preserving Transaction SMS Parser

This document outlines the end-to-end Agile Sprint Plan for building and delivering the **On-Device Privacy-Preserving Transaction SMS Parser SDK**. The project is designed to meet production-grade standards, adhering to strict financial data security practices and the Indian Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023.

---

## 1. Project Roadmap & Milestones

```
[Month 1: Foundation & Local Engine] ────────────────> [Month 2: ML, Security & Production Release]
  ├── Sprint 1: Rust Core & JNI Bindings                 ├── Sprint 3: Differential Privacy & Node.js Backend
  └── Sprint 2: TFLite Classification & Aggregations     └── Sprint 4: Hardening, DPDP Compliance & CI/CD
```

### High-Level Milestones
*   **Milestone 1 (End of Sprint 1):** Functional Kotlin SDK capable of reading device SMS, passing raw text to a secure Rust-compiled library via JNI, and storing parsed transactions in an encrypted SQLCipher database.
*   **Milestone 2 (End of Sprint 2):** On-device TensorFlow Lite model classifying transactional vs. personal messages and executing local aggregation algorithms (Average Daily Balance, Debt-to-Income, Monthly Income).
*   **Milestone 3 (End of Sprint 3):** Fully integrated Node.js billing & ingestion server. Secure, zero-knowledge feature payload upload with license key verification ($0.15/transaction meter active).
*   **Milestone 4 (End of Sprint 4):** Production-ready SDK with <15MB footprint, <1.5% battery consumption overhead, full DPDP compliance, and automated CI/CD pipelines.

