ENGINEERING STANDARDS:
# Engineering Standards & Coding Guidelines
## On-Device Privacy-Preserving Transaction SMS Parser SDK

This document defines the engineering standards, architectural patterns, security protocols, and quality assurance guidelines for the On-Device Privacy-Preserving Transaction SMS Parser SDK. 

---

## 1. Executive Architectural Overview & Privacy Boundaries

The SDK executes on-device to analyze transactional SMS and UPI notification streams, generating a real-time cash flow profile for thin-file MSMEs. 

To comply with Google Play Developer Policies, MeitY regulations (India), and strict privacy-by-design principles, the system enforces an absolute **Data Air-Gap**:

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                  ANDROID DEVICE                                   |
|                                                                                   |
|  +------------------+      +-------------------+      +------------------------+  |
|  |   SMS Receiver   | ---> |  Rust Parser Core | ---> |   TFLite NLP Engine    |  |
|  | (Raw Transaction)|      | (Regex/RegexSet)  |      | (Intent/Entity Class)  |  |
|  +------------------+      +-------------------+      +------------------------+  |
|                                      |                            |               |
|                                      v                            v               |
|                            +-------------------------------------------+          |
|                            |      SQLCipher Local Database (Encrypted)  |          |
|                            +-------------------------------------------+          |
|                                                  |                                |
|                                                  v                                |
|                            +-------------------------------------------+          |
|                            |       Local Cash-Flow Aggregator Engine   |          |
|                            |    (Monthly Income, Avg Daily Bal, DTI)   |          |
|                            +-------------------------------------------+          |
|                                                  |                                |
+--------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------+
                                                   | (Aggregated Metadata Only)
                                                   v [HTTPS / TLS 1.3]
                                     +---------------------------+
                                     |    Node.js Ingestion      |
                                     |     (Lender Backend)      |
                                     +---------------------------+
```

### Core Privacy Constraints
1. **Zero Raw-Data Exfiltration**: Raw SMS body strings, sender addresses, and specific transaction timestamps must never leave the local device boundary.
2. **Local Processing Only**: Parsing, entity extraction, and financial profile aggregation must occur entirely within the local process space using Rust and TensorFlow Lite.
3. **Aggregated Telemetry**: The Node.js backend must only ingest high-level, non-reversible mathematical representations (e.g., monthly transaction velocity, average daily balance, debt-to-income ratio).

---

## 2. Project Directory Structure

The system is structured as a monorepo to coordinate the Android SDK, Native Rust Core, Machine Learning assets, and Node.js ingestion backend.

