- `backend/app/core/kafka.py` — async `KafkaManager` with `start`/`stop`/`send_event`, plus an `InMemoryKafkaBroker` fallback used when `KAFKA_ENABLED=False` or the broker is unreachable (connection failures and timeouts are caught and downgraded gracefully).
- `backend/app/services/profile_service.py` — `apply_profile_update` (used by the API) and `publish_profile_update`/`build_profile_update_event` emit the required JSON schema (`event_id` UUIDv4, `user_id`, `PROFILE_UPDATED`, ISO-8601 timestamp, `payload` with `interests`/`values`/`bio`) and use `str(user_id)` as the partition key.
- `ml-engine/src/services/kafka_consumer.py` — async loop subscribing to `profile-updates` that logs `[Kafka Consumer] Processed profile update event for user: <user_id>`. Runs standalone via `python …/kafka_consumer.py`.
