"test_code": "# Integration tests\n\nThese tests run against a **running** instance of the app. They do not import\nany application code, so they exercise the real HTTP boundary (and the chat\nWebSocket).\n\n## Required env vars\n\n| Var | Default | Purpose |\n|-----|---------|---------|\n| `BASE_URL` | `http://localhost:8000` | Catch-all base URL used when a service-specific URL is not set. |\n| `BACKEND_BASE_URL` | `$BASE_URL` | Aura backend (profiles, privacy). |\n| `AUTH_BASE_URL` | `$BASE_URL` | Auth service (OTP endpoints). |\n| `PAYMENTS_BASE_URL` | `$BASE_URL` | Payments + subscriptions service. |\n| `CHAT_BASE_URL` | `$BASE_URL` | Chat service (HTTP + WS). |\n| `JWT_SECRET_KEY` | `supersecretkeyforlocaldevelopmentonly1234567890` | Must match the running service to mint tokens for protected endpoints. Otherwise auth-required cases are skipped. |\n| `PHONE_HASH_SALT` | `discreet_pepper_salt_value` | Must match the auth service for OTP-derived hashing. |\n| `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | `mock_secret` | Must match the payments service to sign webhook bodies. |\n| `INTEGRATION_TIMEOUT` | `15.0` | Per-request timeout in seconds. |\n\n## Running\n\n```bash\npip install -r tests/integration/requirements.txt\nBASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 pytest tests/integration -v\n```\n\nTests will skip gracefully (rather than fail) when:\n\n- A service's `/health` endpoint is unreachable.\n- The running service uses a different `JWT_SECRET_KEY` or `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` than the defaults, so we can't fabricate valid tokens / signatures.\n- A test needs pre-existing DB state (e.g. a `ChatSession` row) that isn't present.\n"
}
